{"step_index":5491,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T17:03:37Z","thinking":"The system is incorrectly identifying mismatches as auto-matches. Investigation of the auto-match logic reveals a fuzzy matching threshold of 85%. This threshold causes incorrect matches, specifically where similar, but different products are classified as equivalent. For example, 'سينوبريت' and 'سينوبريل', which have an 87.5% similarity score, are incorrectly matched.\n\n\nThe fuzzy matching relies on character similarity, incorrectly matching product names that are similar but have different meanings due to small character variations. The \"safe auto-match\" also fails to accurately compare product strengths because the absence of a strength indicator avoids the check. When form is not specified, form compatibility is considered True.\n\n\nThe discrepancy in numeral representation within the strength string (`١٠/١٦/١٢٤٠` vs. standard) explains the false matches; specifically, the auto-matching rule failed to normalize numerical components. The \"Safety Net\" is overly aggressive, catching almost all candidates due to the `score >= 0.40` condition. The system needs more refined filters.\n\n\nAuto-match (143) success stemmed from exact or normalized-exact brand matches and full token matches, not fuzzy logic. Review (1176) cases arose from brand name discrepancies, numeric format differences, or form incompatibilities (e.g., drops vs. tablets).\n\nCalibration of Level 2 now mandates strict identical or normalized-identical brand matching. Numeric extraction will include Eastern digits and numbers without units. Form incompatibilities are strictly enforced. Candidate pool for the LLM expanded to include the top 5 or 6 matches.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Simulate calibrated matching and review logic on PROC-009 data\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"i