{"step_index":5505,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T17:04:36Z","thinking":"The auto-matcher correctly rejects each problematic case. This outcome confirms the calibration's effectiveness in distinguishing between similar, yet distinct, drug names and strengths. The updated matcher now identifies brand differences and strength discrepancies, indicating improved accuracy.\n\n\nInvestigating the impact of increasing the number of candidate matches provided to the LLM from three to five or six. The rationale is that the correct match may be ranked lower due to minor phrasing differences, which could be resolved by providing more options. Confirmed that the LLM prompt is designed to receive a variable number of candidates.\n\n\nExamining the logic implemented to prevent items from being incorrectly marked as \"no_match,\" particularly when a brand connection exists. This check routes potential matches to a review queue if certain similarity thresholds are met, even if a direct match isn't found, preventing potential mismatches due to minor variations. The objective is to identify if this safety net is functioning as intended to minimize incorrect rejections.\n\n\nThe review queue swelled due to overly broad criteria. The initial conditions, especially the score threshold, caused almost all \"no_match\" LLM responses to trigger review. The implemented brand similarity check allowed unrelated drugs to be marked for review. The correct logic should consider \"same brand\" scenarios, which includes high similarity or common prefixes, for routing to review, not entirely different drugs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Simulate review filtering with proper brand similarity\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\".\\\")\\nimport openpyxl\\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\\nfrom src.fast_match.search import extract_brand_tokens\\n\\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('data/processes/PROC-009/results_PROC-009.xlsx', data_only=True)\\nws_rev = wb['يحتاج مراجعة']\\n\\nrows = []\\nfor r in ws_rev.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\\n    req = str(r[1] or '').strip()\\n    wh = str(r[2] or '').strip()\\n    wh_name = str(r[3] or '').strip()\\n    reason = str(r[4] or '').strip()\\n    if req and wh:\\n        rows.append((req, wh, wh_name, reason))\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Total review pairs in PROC-009: {len(rows)}\\\")\\n\\n# If we filter by brand similarity\\nfor threshold in [85, 80, 75, 70]:\\n    kept = []\\n    dropped = []\\n    for req, wh, wh_name, reason in rows:\\n        b_r = extract_brand_tokens(req)\\n        b_w = extract_brand_tokens(wh)\\n        sim = max(\\n            fuzz.ratio(b_r, b_w),\\n            fuzz.token_sort_ratio(b_r, b_w),\\n            fuzz.ratio(b_r.replace(' ', ''), b_w.replace(' ', ''))\\n        )\\n        # Check first token similarity\\n        w_r = b_r.split()\\n        w_w = b_w.split()\\n        if w_r and w_w and (w_r[0] == w_w[0] or fuzz.ratio(w_r[0], w_w[0]) >= 85):\\n            sim = max(sim, 85)\\n            \\n        if sim >= threshold:\\n            kept.append((sim, req, wh, wh_name))\\n        else:\\n            dropped.append((sim, req, wh, wh_name))\\n            \\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n--- Threshold >= {threshold}% ---\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Kept in Review: {len(kept)}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Filtered out (Not Found in this WH): {len(dropped)}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"Sample kept:\\\")\\n    for sim, req, wh, wh_name in kept[:5]:\\n        print(f\\\"  [{sim}%] {req} vs {wh} ({wh_name})\\\")\\n\"","Description":"\"Simulate thresholding review items\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\scratch\\\\sim_review_filter.py\"","toolAction":"\"Write threshold simulation\"","toolSummary":"\"Threshold simulation script\""}}]}
